A||||2||fiero_nightmare||oil pressure/electric short (2 ?'s)||||1||
Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-18-2001||10:48 PM||||i just got my 85 GT on the road today after changing engines and i found 2 problems with it. <P>1st problem : when i first start driving it it has over 80 pounds of oil pressure but after about 20 minutes i have about 20 pounds of pressure at 1000 RPM. i think it may either be i am using 5W30 oil or a short in the gauge. is it safe to drive it with that low of oil pressure?<P>2nd problem: when i push the electric decklid release the brake light comes on,the oil needle drops slightly,i hear a clicking noise that may be a flasher and the decklid doesn't open. anyone have any idea where i should start looking for the short?<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <BR> <A HREF="http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw" TARGET=_blank>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fiero_nightmare (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||10-18-2001||11:03 PM||||As for the oil pressure..... 5W30 is the recommended oil for the Fiero. My thought is that the sending unit is going bad - it is located on the right side of the engine between the engine and the battery and is mounted vertically -- the plug sits on top of the sender - (the sending unit is about the size of a medium asprin bottle - the top of the sending unit (when unplugged) will have three flat blade contacts (all of this description just in case you are not sure where the sending unit is or what it may look like) I would first replace the sending unit as that is more than likely the problem. (Normal oil pressure on mine is around 70 lbs. in gear)<P>As for the other problem......the cross-car wiring harness that connects all of the components you mentioned is located behind the dash. However, if you have a weak battery you will get most of the symptoms you described. The flasher, by the way, is located under the passenger side of the dash. You may be hearing the deck release solenoid operating but with not enough power to operate the latch. Other than that, it means tracing the wiring and more than likely you will discover a loose ground behind the dash.<P>Hope this helps<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocks_sig.jpg">    </A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero_nightmare||10-18-2001||11:16 PM||||thanks for the quick response.  i have spent all of my money on getting my fiero on the road so i will have to wait about a month to get the sender. now i get to have the fun of taking the dash apart   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">   .  my fiero should be totally done by 10/20/2020   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fiero_nightmare (edited 10-18-2001).]||||reg||1
